<%# Grade books, full width under the roster rather than a 256px rail beside it.

    It was `w-64 flex-initial` in a `lg:flex-row` with the roster, which is the shape Polaris calls a
    secondary column - and Polaris is explicit that the secondary column carries *supporting* detail
    (status, tags, metadata), not a second collection. Two collections side by side makes the narrower
    one look subordinate while giving the wider one less room than it needs: at 1366px the roster had
    about 760px for four columns including two currency figures.

    Stacked full-width sections are what the field does for an entity's related collections - Stripe's
    customer page (payments, then subscriptions, then invoices), GitHub's repository page, Linear's
    project page. Each gets a heading and the full column width, and the reading order says which is
    primary rather than the widths.

    Four quarters across at lg, one column below it. A quarter is a destination, not a row of data, so
    each is a card-sized target with its state on it - which the 256px list could not show. `status` is
    a real enum (draft / verified / completed) that the rail never surfaced, so a teacher could not see
    which quarters were done without opening all four. %>
<% tones = { "draft" => :neutral, "verified" => :info, "completed" => :success } %>

<section aria-labelledby="grade-books-heading">
  <h2 id="grade-books-heading" class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900">Grade books</h2>
  <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-600">
    One per quarter. Open a quarter to record attendance and grades, which is what pays students their
    funds to invest.
  </p>

  <div class="mt-3">
    <% if grade_books.any? %>
      <ul class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 lg:grid-cols-4">
        <% grade_books.each do |book| %>
          <li>
            <%# The whole card is the link, so the target is the card and not a word inside it. %>
            <%= link_to classroom_grade_book_path(@classroom, book),
                        class: "tw-card flex items-center justify-between gap-3 p-5 transition-colors " \
                               "hover:bg-slate-50 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 " \
                               "focus-visible:outline-sitf-primary" do %>
              <span class="min-w-0">
                <span class="block text-sm font-medium text-slate-900"><%= book.quarter.name %></span>
                <span class="mt-1 block">
                  <%= render "components/ui/badge",
                             label: book.status.capitalize,
                             tone: tones.fetch(book.status, :neutral) %>
                </span>
              </span>
              <%= lucide_icon("arrow-right", class: "size-4 shrink-0 text-slate-500") %>
            <% end %>
          </li>
        <% end %>
      </ul>
    <% else %>
      <%= render layout: "components/ui/card", locals: { padded: false } do %>
        <%= render layout: "components/ui/empty_state",
                   locals: { icon: "book", compact: true,
                             title: "No grade books yet",
                             body: "They appear here once the school year's quarters have them." } do %>
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</section>
